WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.300
The operating rule is one front door.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.112
Nothing is handled as an
email to the cloud team.

3
00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:08.798
Portal requests, emails,
identity governance tasks

4
00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:12.399
and monitoring alerts all
land in one triage queue.

5
00:00:12.399 --> 00:00:16.488
Triage asks one question: what
authority does this task need?

6
00:00:16.488 --> 00:00:19.212
That answer picks the
pipeline and the approver,

7
00:00:19.212 --> 00:00:23.025
from a simple fix up to governance
actions that are never automated.

8
00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:26.594
One small rule matters: if
an approver doesn't respond,

9
00:00:26.594 --> 00:00:30.163
the request is rejected or
cancelled, never approved.

10
00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.026
Silence can't grant access.

11
00:00:32.026 --> 00:00:36.659
The decision for the service desk
manager: close the side doors, route the

12
00:00:36.659 --> 00:00:41.525
team mailbox into triage, and count any
work done outside it as a measured gap.

13
00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:43.320
Next, what the desk may do.
